and the shooting comes just one day  after education secretary Betsy DeVos  met with a group behind closed doors the  White House survivors and other family  members affected by school shootings the  meeting was supposed to help lay the  groundwork for the administration's new  school safety commission well Jay T  Lewis was part of that meeting he  tragically lost his brother in Sandy  Hook he joins us now live to talk about  where we go from here JT thanks for  joining us tonight thanks for having me  what's your reaction today I mean you've  been through this numerous times hearing  this news since the day you lost your  brother and I know you're frustrated  because you think there are things we  can be doing and we're not doing yeah I  I just feel so bad for all the victims I  know exactly what they're going through  it's it's the rest of your life will be  spent in pain and it's unfortunate  because there are things we can do to  prevent these shootings so we hear from  Education Secretary Betsy DeVos we  simply cannot allow this trend to  continue our work remains urgent our  nation must come together and address  the underlying issues that lead to such  tragic and senseless loss of life very  similar language from the House Minority  Leader Democrat Nancy Pelosi saying no  other community or family must endure  the unthinkable horror of gun violence  our children deserve real leadership a  vote to prevent gun violence now so what  in your estimation is out there you're  part of this conversation with this  effort to find real world solutions what  can be done yeah well first I just want  to take a minute to thank Secretary  teuvos for holding that meeting and for  hearing from members of the community  people who've been affected by these  shootings to get the best possible  information compile it into report  return it to the President and then take  it from there and you know get things  done to stop the shooting it's it's  getting ridiculous at this point but a  few things that I would like to see my  biggest thing is armed guards and  schools  you see schools where there are armed  guards three of the most recent  shootings one in Illinois recently maybe  just Friday where an armed guard  confronts the student apprehension  sometimes a student doesn't even die and  the casualties are kept to one or zero  and that's still too many but it's  better than 17 in parkland 26 in Newtown  a university professor from Northeastern  University his name is James Ellen Fox  he studies these math school shootings  he himself is a proponent of gun control  but he talks about the fact that when  you talk about armed guards or armed  teachers or other safety measures he  worries about the impact he says this  I'm not a big fan of making schools look  like fortresses because they send a  message to kids that the bad guy is  coming for you if we're surrounding you  with security you must have a bull's-eye  on your back and that can actually  instill fear not relieve it as a young  person yourself what do you think of  that well I've talked to my classmates  about this I've talked to a lot of  different people  the idea of armed guards has a lot of  support and I just want to say after  9/11 Airport sided security they did it  because it keeps us safe and it's the  same thing in schools and you get used  to it you know and schools will add the  security will add metal detectors will  add single entry points will add armed  guards and over time we will get used to  it it's for our own safety it's for the  safety of our youth well I know that the  number of armed guards has gone up this  the numbers show us that the studies  show us that and I know it's you're  gonna be a part of this continuing  conversation with this group as they try  to come up with solid answers to this  and there don't seem to be any easy ones  they're gonna take some fighting and  some you know uphill battles to get them  done but we're glad your voice is in the  conversation I can only imagine all of  the emotions you go through today I know  it's your birthday as well so JT thank  you for making time for us and for  continuing to try to be a voice in this  process thank you for having me
 

